    "state_protocol": "prepare(context, request) applies the source's numerical policy via the equivalent of common.configure (torch.set_num_threads(4), interop threads 1, TF32 disabled for matmul and cudnn, cudnn.benchmark off, float32_matmul_precision 'highest'), seeds torch.manual_seed(20261020), builds GPT2LMHeadModel from request['workload']['model'] dimensions with resid_pdrop=embd_pdrop=attn_pdrop=0.0, use_cache=False, attn_implementation='eager', moves it to context['device'], wraps it in DDP(broadcast_buffers=False, bucket_cap_mb=25, gradient_as_bucket_view=True) using the bound device (no new process group; the worker already initialized it), creates SGD(lr=0.001, momentum=0.0, weight_decay=0.0, foreach=False), generates this rank's micro-batches once with torch.Generator().manual_seed(31000 + rank), snapshots the initial raw_model.state_dict() to CPU, and creates the source's auxiliary gloo control group. state holds raw_model, the DDP-wrapped model, optimizer, GPU-resident inputs, the initial CPU snapshot, the workload dict, device, rank and world_size. reset(state) reloads the initial CPU state_dict into the raw model outside timing; it deliberately does not clear gradients or optimizer state because the source performs zero_grad(set_to_none=True) inside the timed step and SGD(momentum=0) carries no persistent state, so each measured unit starts exactly from the seed-20261020 initial weights. run(state) executes the full frozen step (see completion) and returns the summed scaled loss tensor. observe(state, result) returns detached CPU clones of the loss, every named parameter gradient after the allreduce, and every post-update named parameter. metrics(state, result, elapsed_ms) returns the source's clean project metrics in native units: step_ms from elapsed_ms, tokens_per_second from the unchanged 1024-token step, peak_allocated_bytes from torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated() (framework resets peak stats immediately before its timer), plus loss, effective_